{"name":"Classic Cool","hex":"#b7b2ac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"classic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to the first class or rank, especially in literature or art.","Exemplary of a particular style; defining a class or category; typical; archetypical; epitomic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perfect and/or early example of a particular style.","An artistic work of lasting worth, such as a film or song; a work of enduring excellence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classic"},{"term":"cool","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a mildly low temperature.","Allowing or suggesting heat relief."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A moderate or refreshing state of cold; moderate temperature of the air between hot and cold; coolness.","A calm temperament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool"}],"entries":[{"title":"Classic","blocks":[{"text":"A classic is an outstanding example of a particular style; something of lasting worth or with a timeless quality; of the first or highest quality, class, or rank – something that exemplifies its class. The word can be an adjective or a noun. It denotes a particular quality in art, architecture, literature, design, technology, or other cultural artifacts. In commerce, products are named 'classic' to denote a long-standing popular version or model, to distinguish it from a newer variety. Classic is used to describe many major, long-standing sporting events. Colloquially, an everyday occurrence may be described in some dialects of English as 'an absolute classic'."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classic","wikidata":"Q2976603"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"classic":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav.ogg"}],"cool":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f7/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f7/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cool.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey bucchero-ware bowl, Clay, 1000-700 BCE, Nr. Babakõy, Turkey, Fitzwilliam Museum, Cambridge","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg/500px-Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg","ratio":0.8,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl,_Clay,_1000-700_BCE,_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y,_Turkey,_Fitzwilliam_Museum,_Cambridge.jpg","share":0.644375},{"title":"Madeira Grey Cat","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Madeira_Grey_Cat.JPG/500px-Madeira_Grey_Cat.JPG","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madeira_Grey_Cat.JPG","share":0.24875},{"title":"Grey Carpet from above","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg/500px-Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg","s